ce here is to do any processing with the laptop. Of course you can find, is this laptop good for programming or is this laptop good for gaming? So you can have those type of methods in the service class, but at this point I don't have that class. So I can just create that class here. So I can say laptop service class, service, equal to context dot get bean, laptop service dot class. But unfortunately we don't have this class, so let's create one. So I can just click here and say, hey, IDE, I want to get a laptop class, laptop service class, and this should be a part of a service package. So you have to make sure that you keep your classes in the right package. It will not give you error, but if you have your classes in separate packages, it will be easier for you to manage them and find them. So let's put that service in service package and now you can see there's no problem. The only problem is we don't have this particular method. So we can say add laptop. As I mentioned before, we can return a boolean, it is good for programming. So maybe we can create some methods like this. So pass a laptop object and we can return whatever the configuration is. So you can, based on the configuration, you can return if it is good or bad. So at this point, I'm just returning true, but you got the idea right? So service will be having certain methods where you can do some processing part, okay? But then we don't want to worry about this method. I want to worry about the add laptop. So in this add laptop, what I wanna do, is I want to add the laptop in the database, right? But this is your service class right. Now, if you want to get this object, which annotation are we going to use here, because what we are doing in this is we are saying that context dot get bean laptop service. This will not work if you don't have add component on top of it. But as I mentioned before, add component is not the only option. If you want to work with service class, we can also use service stereotype. Now, service and component does the same thing. They both say it becomes a managed bean because if you click on service, you can see service itself is added with component, okay? It is just that if you want to create some documentation or if you're writing some domain specific language or application, it makes sense to use service on top of it. It also helps you to understand what type of class you're working with, okay? So when you have add service on top of it, you can understand that is service class. Again, even if you write add component, you will not get the error. It will work. But using service makes much more sense. But the kind of application which we are building, everything is same, okay? There's no difference between component and service. So for different purposes you can differentiate between component and service. At this point, they both are same. Will behave the same way. Okay, so now let's see if this works. I will just print here, method called, and let's see if this works. Let's run this. And okay, it says method called, there's some issue with my IDE, which is not resolved yet. Maybe I have to update the IDE anyway. So you can say, it says method called. So service is working. Apart from this, what if you want to store this data in database, you want to store this lap in database? In this case, where you will write your database steps. Of course, when you say database steps, remember when we talked about JDBC? So if you want to connect your Java application with database, we need JDBC in between, which is Java database connectivity, where you will write your JDBC steps inside service class. You can, of course there is no harm, I mean there is harm, but there's no error when you do that. But it's not a good practice. Where you should write your JDBC code is a separate class called repository class, where you will have all the database connections. The only job of that class is to work with database. The job of service is to process the data or do some processing on some objects and something, but not connecting with database. So when you will do it, we'll do that in the next video and that in different class."
